WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.241 --> 00:00:13.823
On the surface, everything at the March home appeared to return to normal.

2
00:00:14.843 --> 00:00:19.586
Amy was back home, showing off her ring (not mentioning to Meg that she had left it to

3
00:00:19.646 --> 00:00:25.689
her in her will) and entertaining the family with funny episodes about Aunt March and her parrot, Polly.

4
00:00:26.629 --> 00:00:33.597
Beneath the smiles and laughter, however, the sisters had changed considerably; they were no longer the carefree young

5
00:00:33.637 --> 00:00:35.777
girls they used to be before Beth's illness.

6
00:00:36.857 --> 00:00:39.938
Perhaps the person who changed the most was Beth herself.

7
00:00:40.959 --> 00:00:44.600
Outwardly, she seemed to regain her health and sunny disposition.

8
00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:51.942
Her optimistic and innocent world, however, had been shattered when the Hummel baby died in her arms, giving

9
00:00:51.982 --> 00:00:53.682
Beth a close encounter with death.

10
00:00:54.863 --> 00:00:59.744
Beth withdrew even more into herself as if an inner light in her had been switched off.

11
00:01:01.308 --> 00:01:06.870
Seeing the change in Beth, Jo knew that she could never forgive herself for contributing to the loss

12
00:01:06.910 --> 00:01:08.370
of happiness in her sister's life.

13
00:01:08.390 --> 00:01:11.571
"Jo? Jo!"

14
00:01:12.131 --> 00:01:13.091
Amy called sharply.

15
00:01:14.412 --> 00:01:18.113
Lost in thought, Jo did not even hear Amy speaking to her.

16
00:01:18.133 --> 00:01:20.374
"Sorry, Amy.

17
00:01:20.854 --> 00:01:21.614
What did you say?"

18
00:01:21.874 --> 00:01:22.354
she asked.

19
00:01:22.374 --> 00:01:25.715
"I asked, 'Where is Laurie?'

20
00:01:26.095 --> 00:01:33.049
He was incredibly faithful," said Amy, "visiting me every day at Aunt March's so I wouldn't go insane

21
00:01:33.069 --> 00:01:33.689
with worry.

22
00:01:34.669 --> 00:01:36.850
Without him, I would have died!"

23
00:01:38.190 --> 00:01:44.152
Then realizing her poor choice of words, she quickly added, "I mean, it would have been just awful!"

24
00:01:44.172 --> 00:01:47.013
"Am I his keeper?"

25
00:01:47.393 --> 00:01:48.693
barked Jo spitefully.

26
00:01:48.713 --> 00:01:52.674
"Frankly, Laurie is the least of my concerns now.

27
00:01:53.535 --> 00:01:56.715
My thoughts are occupied with far more important matters at the moment."

28
00:01:58.116 --> 00:02:04.600
Meg, noticing Jo's peculiar response, knew that her sister was not on speaking terms with Laurie because of

29
00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:06.121
the tasteless joke he had played.

30
00:02:07.122 --> 00:02:12.046
Meg also knew that Jo, although she was pretending to the world and herself that it didn't matter,

31
00:02:12.526 --> 00:02:14.827
was deeply troubled by the rift in their friendship.

32
00:02:14.847 --> 00:02:21.772
"I think we should have Laurie and his grandfather over for dinner tonight," Meg suggested while she looked

33
00:02:21.812 --> 00:02:23.634
away from Jo's piercing glare.

34
00:02:23.654 --> 00:02:25.355
"Why should we?"

35
00:02:25.655 --> 00:02:26.556
Jo asked sharply.

36
00:02:27.476 --> 00:02:33.078
"Jo! You ought to be ashamed of yourself after all the Laurences have done for us," scolded Amy

37
00:02:33.138 --> 00:02:37.660
righteously. "We are indebted to them forever for their selfless deeds."

38
00:02:39.241 --> 00:02:43.583
"I agree with Meg," said Mother, giving Amy a warning look to go easy on Jo.

39
00:02:43.603 --> 00:02:47.544
"We should invite them this evening if they're available."

40
00:02:47.564 --> 00:02:50.326
"Can I ask Laurie myself?"

41
00:02:50.726 --> 00:02:53.167
Amy jumped up, clapping her hands like a little girl.

42
00:02:54.267 --> 00:02:57.465
Glancing at Jo, Mother replied, "Yes, you may."

43
00:02:58.886 --> 00:03:04.229
When Mother and Amy left together with Meg trailing closely behind, Beth turned to her sister with worried

44
00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:07.732
eyes and asked, "Is everything all right with you and Laurie?"

45
00:03:09.013 --> 00:03:13.916
Pressing her lips together, Jo forced a smile and took Beth's pale, thin hand.

46
00:03:13.936 --> 00:03:20.360
"Friendships are forged through time, experience, and overcoming obstacles.

47
00:03:21.401 --> 00:03:27.369
Laurie and I have hit a barrier at the moment," Jo said truthfully, "but I'm confident that we

48
00:03:27.409 --> 00:03:28.290
will get over this."

49
00:03:29.571 --> 00:03:33.253
Squeezing her hand gently, Beth rested her head on Jo's shoulder.

50
00:03:36.015 --> 00:03:41.259
On such short notice, a lot of tightly organized teamwork was needed to put together a meal quickly.

51
00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:47.804
For the rest of the day, everyone busily took charge of certain tasks to ensure a highly hospitable

52
00:03:47.904 --> 00:03:48.845
evening for their neighbors.

53
00:03:48.865 --> 00:03:51.807
"It's half-past six already!

54
00:03:52.067 --> 00:03:53.348
They'll be here any minute!"

55
00:03:53.736 --> 00:03:56.337
Amy panicked as she set the cutlery on the table.

56
00:03:56.357 --> 00:03:59.898
"Meg, did you check the potatoes?"

57
00:04:00.198 --> 00:04:02.098
Mother asked as she rushed toward the kitchen.

58
00:04:02.118 --> 00:04:09.220
"They're all done," answered Meg, careful not to collide with Mother as she carried out a large steaming

59
00:04:09.260 --> 00:04:16.602
dish. While the others scrambled around the kitchen, Jo volunteered to help Beth downstairs so she could join

60
00:04:16.622 --> 00:04:17.323
the festivities.

61
00:04:17.343 --> 00:04:25.779
"My legs feel like rubber," giggled Beth as she struggled to maintain her balance on shaky legs.

62
00:04:25.799 --> 00:04:31.264
"Just hang on to me," said Jo, holding Beth around the waist and arm.

63
00:04:32.646 --> 00:04:39.192
Her progress was painstakingly slow, but in the end Beth managed to seat herself on the sofa, then

64
00:04:39.292 --> 00:04:41.574
Jo wrapped a thick blanket around her for warmth.

65
00:04:42.735 --> 00:04:46.538
As Beth smiled up at her sister, there was a knock at the door, and Jo was the

66
00:04:46.618 --> 00:04:48.060
only one available to answer it.

67
00:04:50.260 --> 00:04:51.041
"Good evening, Mr.

68
00:04:51.061 --> 00:04:54.522
Laurence," Jo greeted Laurie's grandfather as she opened the door.

69
00:04:55.763 --> 00:04:58.665
She merely nodded to Laurie, who returned the curt gesture.

70
00:04:59.925 --> 00:05:05.909
Mr. Laurence immediately made his way toward Beth, who welcomed her dear friend with a weak but genuine

71
00:05:05.949 --> 00:05:11.091
smile. Standing together awkwardly, Laurie and Jo spoke at the same time.

72
00:05:11.111 --> 00:05:12.832
"So how.

73
00:05:12.852 --> 00:05:15.854
"What did.

74
00:05:15.894 --> 00:05:17.355
"You go first," said Jo.

75
00:05:17.375 --> 00:05:20.216
"It's nothing," replied Laurie.

76
00:05:20.236 --> 00:05:26.258
"Laurie!" Amy shouted cheerfully as she ran over to him and threw her arms around his neck.

77
00:05:27.438 --> 00:05:31.139
Grateful for the interruption, Jo escaped to help Meg set the table.

78
00:05:32.139 --> 00:05:38.061
Dinner talk was light and full of laughter—the main entertainment was Amy, who repeated her stories from Aunt

79
00:05:38.101 --> 00:05:44.123
March's. If anyone noticed the tension between Laurie and Jo, they did not mention it.

80
00:05:44.143 --> 00:05:47.504
"Jo, can you bring some more bread from the oven?"

81
00:05:47.804 --> 00:05:48.764
Mother asked kindly.

82
00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:54.284
Jo stood up, grabbed the bread basket and was heading toward the kitchen when she overheard Mr.

83
00:05:54.324 --> 00:05:58.247
Laurence saying, "Laurie, can you bring me a glass of water?"

84
00:05:59.908 --> 00:06:03.371
Even though Mother protested that one of the girls could get it, Mr.

85
00:06:03.391 --> 00:06:08.875
Laurence insisted his grandson should go, thereby driving Laurie into the kitchen where Jo was.

86
00:06:09.715 --> 00:06:14.899
Trying to ignore him, Jo tossed the bread into the basket as quickly as she could without acknowledging

87
00:06:14.939 --> 00:06:15.520
his presence.

88
00:06:16.576 --> 00:06:21.218
But since they were thrown together in a situation like this, they couldn't avoid talking.

89
00:06:21.238 --> 00:06:24.119
"Jo?" Laurie spoke first.

90
00:06:25.240 --> 00:06:26.620
She turned to him without speaking.

91
00:06:26.640 --> 00:06:30.562
"I don't know how to make things right," he said quietly.

92
00:06:30.582 --> 00:06:34.283
"Could you forgive me and accept me as a friend again?"

93
00:06:35.124 --> 00:06:39.326
Jo felt a lump in her throat as she looked at Laurie bowing his head, staring down at

94
00:06:39.346 --> 00:06:39.866
his hands.

95
00:06:41.446 --> 00:06:44.828
All her animosity, anger, and hurt melted away in an instant.

96
00:06:46.028 --> 00:06:49.510
"Silly boy," she mumbled, "of course I can."

97
00:06:50.611 --> 00:06:53.913
Jo grabbed him roughly by the neck and playfully messed up his hair.

98
00:06:53.933 --> 00:06:57.535
"I'm really sorry, Jo," Laurie said sincerely.

99
00:06:57.555 --> 00:07:01.077
"Let's just forget about it," said Jo.

100
00:07:02.758 --> 00:07:06.660
The two friends smiled at each other and knew that everything was going to be fine.

101
00:07:07.421 --> 00:07:12.604
Suddenly a loud commotion arose from the living room, forcing Jo and Laurie to cut short their reunion.

102
00:07:13.804 --> 00:07:19.047
Meg and Amy were beside themselves as they ran toward a tall thin man standing in the doorway.

103
00:07:19.067 --> 00:07:21.629
"Father! Father!"

104
00:07:21.829 --> 00:07:26.712
they screamed, as Mother stood still at the table, wiping her eyes with her napkin.

105
00:07:26.732 --> 00:07:33.596
"I'm home, my little girls," said Father happily as he hugged and kissed each of his daughters.

106
00:07:34.776 --> 00:07:35.937
Behind him stood Mr.

107
00:07:35.957 --> 00:07:40.900
Brookes, quiet as ever, but staring at only one person in the room: Meg.

108
00:07:42.108 --> 00:07:46.771
Lifting Beth from her chair and putting her on his lap, Father gathered his girls around him and

109
00:07:46.811 --> 00:07:49.172
said, "How I missed my little women."

110
00:07:50.613 --> 00:07:51.113
When Mr.

111
00:07:51.133 --> 00:07:52.274
Laurence, Laurie, and Mr.

112
00:07:52.334 --> 00:07:56.176
Brookes tried to leave unnoticed, Father called out, "Please stay.

113
00:07:56.696 --> 00:07:59.798
Tonight we're celebrating with both family and friends."

114
00:08:01.439 --> 00:08:03.400
And that is exactly what they did.
